1 NOTE 1840, while living with his parents in Nauvoo, Ill. He experienced the persecutions of the Saints at this time. He was one of the honored pioneers whose early life was made eventful by his close touch
2 CONC  with the Prophet Joseph Smith.
2 CONT After expulsion of the Saints from Nauvoo, he started West with an early migration of Saints. Reaching Council Bluffs, he remained there until 1842. when he, with his mother and only living sister Mar
2 CONC garet and youngest brother Samuel, came on in Heber C. Kimball’s Company to Utah.
2 CONT The first location of the family was at Bountiful, Utah. After 1860, he moved to Millville, Cache Co., Utah, where his ability as a colonizer and integrity as a Saint were marked with honor.
2 CONT 1860, Millville, Cache Co., Utah; m Robert A. Birch.
2 CONT 1895], d. 8 Feb. 1928; m. Joseph O. Davis.
