1 NOTE 1920
2 CONT ; m. Marion Loretta M. Knowles, b. in Pennsylvania. He had his name changed to Daniel Kelly by the Los Angeles Courts 24 Jan. 1939; the record does not state why he had his name changed from Bell to K
2 CONC elly. He graduated from Price High School; trained as a flyer at Price and at Grand Junction, Colo.; attended flying school at Los Angeles; flew at Mines Field, Calif., and trained students for World 
2 CONC War II; was superintendent on one shift at Times air craft during the war.
2 CONT 1920]; m. abt. 1935, Ernest Eugene Sleeth. He was b. 10 May 1910, in
2 CONT Indianapolis, Ind. Mary Elzina is a high school graduate. She graduated also from Los Angeles County Hospital as a nurse and is now doing surgical nursing in Los Angeles. She was supervisor of Downey
2 CONC Hospital during World War II for several years; is also skilled in other lines of work. They had 2 children, b. in Los Angeles, Calif.:
