1 NAME Marietta /Henrie/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 OCT 1892
2 PLAC Ferron, Emery Co., Utah
3 MAP
4 LATI N39.093
4 LONG W111.131
2 NOTE As written: 7 Oct. 1892
1 NOTE In Sept. of that year Marietta and her father returned to Ferron to dispose of the farm and to take back some cows. one day he was feeding the stock and was struck in the ribs by one of the colts jump
2 CONC ing and striking him with its leg or hoof. Two broken bones necessitated his lying around for a time till he was able to travel. When he was able he drove the wagon and team and Marietta rode a horse 
2 CONC and drove the cows the entire distance to LaSal.
2 CONT At LaSal Marietta met Oscar Devon LeaMaster, who with his family had moved to LaSal from Moab, Utah. They commenced keeping company in 1919. He was called to fill a mission for the church in 1920, wit
2 CONC h headquarters in the central states, where he labored for 2 years. They were married in 1923 and lived in LaSal for some time before moving to Hiawatha. Oscar worked in a coal mine, first as a digger
2 CONC , but soon advanced to a nipper, a motorman, then to cutting and loading machines.
2 CONT In 1928 they bought a farm and orchard at Ferron and besides regular farming raised fruit and livestock. Here he served as secretary and then president of the Elders Quorum, then as 2nd counselor in t
2 CONC he Bishopric. In the spring of 1938 his father died and they went to Provo for the funeral. They decided to move there, since the doctor had advised him to quit hard farm labor. They located in the Ma
2 CONC navu Ward and Oscar taught the Gospel Doctrine class and was Ward teacher; Marietta was made 2nd counselor in the Primary. In 1939 they bought a home in the Pioneer Ward.
2 CONT As their family grew up, they felt the need for a larger place than a house and lot and bought 5 acres of land in Springville. The boys, however, were not inclined along the lines of farming and lives
2 CONC tock but preferred to use their brains and hands along mechanical lines. Oscar later worked at the State Hospital as an attendant and was promoted to a supervisor. He resigned this position to work fo
2 CONC r Sears Roebuck & Co., at Provo, as a salesman. He soon became division manager of the farm department and then went into the furniture department.
2 CONT As members of 2nd Ward, Kolob Stake in Springville, Oscar worked in the Y.M.M.I.A. as second counselor. Marietta was Primary chorister, Relief Society chorister, as work meeting class leader and visit
2 CONC ing teacher in Relief Society. She belonged to Camp Aaron Johnson D.U.P., acting as secretary to this camp.
