2 DATE 22 NOV 1917
2 PLAC Moab, Grand Co., Utah
3 MAP
4 LATI N38.573
4 LONG W109.55
2 NOTE As written: 22 Nov. 1917
1 NOTE Beth Rae was blessed with a mother who possessed a most congenial nature and a kind loving disposition. She saw to it that her family were provided with suitable companions and their home was one of l
2 CONC ove and happiness. Three years after her graduation from high school she went to Los Angeles, Calif., to work for a doctor and his wife; later she went to San Diego and worked as a maid in the home of
2 CONC  a millionaire. Beth and Alva had become acquainted while he was in the C.C.C. camp at Ferron, Utah. After his father’s death he went to San Diego, where he found work which enabled him to assist his 
2 CONC mother and young brothers and sisters. Here they met again and soon returned to Ferron where they were married at her mother’s home. They returned to San Diego, then to Los Vegas where Alva worked for
2 CONC  Basic Magnesium. They moved once again to San Diego, where they have resided the past 9 years.
2 CONT Alva was in the National Guard Unit Field Artillery and served 9 years. In 1936 he enrolled in the C.C.C. at Mt. Pleasant, Utah, but due to his father’s death he was given his discharge.
2 CONT During his youth and while a member of the Y.M.M.I.A. Alva became a 2nd grade scout. Some time during his earlier life he was a tuna fisherman for 7 years and was in all the South American countries.
