1 NAME Christena Elfa /Riggs/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 DEC 1897
2 PLAC Panguitch, Utah
3 MAP
4 LATI N37.823
4 LONG W112.436
2 NOTE As written: 19 Dec. 1897
1 NOTE Christena Elfa was b. in a new brick house just built by her parents. It was an extremely cold winter and the snow fell so deep it covered the tops of the fences. Her mother died when she was 7 years
2 CONC old. She was taken to live with her Aunt Sarah (Henrie) Dodds for 2 years. Then her father remarried a widow woman with 4 daughters. There were 10 of them in the house. After grade school she attended
2 CONC  high school for 2 years. She went to work in the Panguitch Co-op store for 2 years; then she helped her father in his cafe. Christena Elfa m. William (Bill) Crosby Tebbs during World War I; he was dr
2 CONC afted in the Army but served only 5 months when the armistice was signed and he returned home. In 1925 Bill was called on a mission to the Eastern States and Elfa took a job in a store. Her health was
2 CONC  not good, but she carried on while he was away. They eventually had means to buy a nice brick home and moved out of the 2 small rooms they had occupied. They had 4 children, all b. in Panguitch:
2 CONT Myrtle graduated from Brigham Young High school and gave the
2 CONT 1949, S.to P. July 1947].
2 CONT Manly Erastus & Mary Arminta (Harper) Sackett. She was b. 15 Mar. 1924,
2 CONT Brigham City, Box Elder Co., Utah. Jack attended elementary schools at Panguitch and high school, after which he enrolled at Brigham Young University, and later the University of Utah. In 1943 he was
2 CONC inducted into the Army, and after completing his basic training he was sent to the University of Calif. School of Dentistry where he received his D.D.S. He practiced in Hawthorne until Feb. 1952, when
2 CONC  he was called back into the Army. He served as Capt. in the Dental Corps for 2 years. They had 3 children
2 CONT 1953].
