1 NOTE Mark Kay graduated from Panguitch High School; he also completed a course of study at National Automotive & Electrical, and Los Angeles Trade School at Los Angeles, Calif. He has been actively engaged
2 CONC  in the business field; has managed a theater house at Panguitch, a Parts and Service Dept. for Lunt Motor, in Cedar City, and at present is manager of Ruynal Buick, in Richfield, Utah. He was a chart
2 CONC er member of the Panguitch Junior Chamber of Commerce and served as vice-president. He was supt. of the Ward M.I.A. at Cedar City for 2 years and at present is activity counselor in the Sevier Stake M
