1 NOTE Bergetta graduated from Garfield High School. She then attended the L.D.S. Business College at Salt Lake City and was given a position as stenographer and bookkeeper in the Panguitch State Bank, where
2 CONC  she worked for 2 ½ years. After her marriage she worked intermittently for the Treasurer of Iron County. For the past 6 years she has been Bookkeeper and Teller in the Bank of Iron County, at Parowan
2 CONC . She has held several responsible positions in her church. For 4 years she was bookkeeper for the Stake Welfare of Parowan Stake; has been a teacher in almost every organization; secretary for Stake 
2 CONC and Ward Primary, and Stake Beekeeper in the M.I.A. Since her husband’s death she has had to readjust her life. She realizes that each child needs both parents and it is not easy to rear children alon
2 CONC e.
2 CONT Jared Johnson Orton grew up in Parowan and attended grade and high school there. He was reared in a good L.D.S home. As his father died when he was 6 years old, he was practically reared by his mother
2 CONC . He was an active Elder in the church, a good husband and father, and had many friends. He had been working for, the Southern Utah Dairy for 10 years at the time of his death.
2 CONT High School and L.D.S. Seminary; she has taught in Primary; has been secretary of Sunday School, and assistant chorister in the M.I.A. Reid Gower graduated from Cedar High School; he joined the Nation
2 CONC al Guard 26 Dec. 1940; entered active service 3 Mar. 1941 and spent 43 months in the Hawaiian Islands as Technician 4th Grade (radio operator). He received an honorable discharge in Oct. 1945. He is a
2 CONC  carpenter and builder by trade. Reid & Lewen (Orton) Gower had 2 children, b. in Cedar City, Utah:
