1 NOTE Artemisia attended High School at Tropic, Panguitch, and Provo, Utah; she also attended Brigham Young University. She taught for years in Primary, Sunday School, and M.I.A.; class leader in Relief Soc
2 CONC iety; served 5 years as 1st councilor in Y.L.M.I.A. in Delta 2nd Ward; served 5 years as 1st councilor of Deseret Stake Relief Society.
2 CONT Warren went 4 years to the L.D.S. High School at Salt Lake City, and attended 3 years at University of Utah and the Utah State Agricultural College. He filled two missions for the L.D.S. Church; first
2 CONC , Swiss-German Mission, and second, Southern States Mission. He served 15 years consecutively in Delta 2nd Ward and the Deseret Stake; served 5 years as Ward Clerk; 2 years as 2nd Councilor; 4 years a
2 CONC s Bishop; was set apart as 2nd Councilor in the Presidency of Deseret Stake, 10 June 1945 and served 5 years; he is now acting as President of the High Priests Quorum of Deseret Stake.
2 CONT Dorothy graduated from Delta High School, where she was prominent in
2 CONT Jonel graduated from Delta High School and Seminary with high honors;
