1 NOTE evidently fell asleep. Irene saw that the machine was going to leave the road and took the wheel and steered it back onto the road. This awakened the driver, who, with a start, gave the wheel a sharp
2 CONC turn and tipped the car over, throwing her 25 to 30 feet, breaking her neck and cutting a dep hole in her head. She died just before they got her to the doctor. Her body was brought to Panguitch and s
2 CONC he was buried in the family burial plot.
2 CONT Everyone loved Irene. She was mild and good, beautiful in looks and actions. She had good habits and tried to do good wherever she went. Her pals talk of her yet and tell how they miss her and her lov
2 CONC ely personality.
